1:#!/usr/bin/env python3
2:#
3:#  lcaisalane -- RUNG-3 WITNESS: the LCA sparse-I/O byte-lane handler ends the host process on an
4:#  ordinary byte access to a documented ISA register, and SILENTLY ANSWERS ZERO on another.
5:#
6:#  THE DEFECT, quoted from `DEVICE_ACCESS(lca_isa)' in src/devices/dev_lca.c:
7:#
8:#      relative_addr >>= 5;
9:#
10:#      ofs = relative_addr & 3;
11:#      if (ofs > len) {
12:#              fatal("[ ofs=%i len=%i in lca_isa access function. "
13:#                  "aborting ]\n", ofs, len);
14:#              exit(1);
15:#      }
16:#
17:#      if (writeflag == MEM_WRITE) {
18:#              byte = data[ofs % len];
19:#              return cpu->memory_rw(cpu, cpu->mem, LCA_ISA_BASE +
20:#                  relative_addr, &byte, 1, writeflag, CACHE_NONE);
21:#      }
22:#
23:#      cpu->memory_rw(cpu, cpu->mem, LCA_ISA_BASE + relative_addr,
24:#          &byte, 1, MEM_READ, CACHE_NONE);
25:#
26:#      for (i=0; i<len; i++)
27:#              data[i] = i == ofs? byte : 0x00;
28:#
29:#  *** THE LANE IS NOT AN INDEPENDENT FIELD.  IT IS THE LOW TWO BITS OF THE ISA PORT NUMBER. ***
30:#  The shift comes FIRST, so `ofs' is bits 6:5 of the incoming relative address -- which are bits
31:#  1:0 of the derived port -- and the forwarded access goes to `LCA_ISA_BASE + (r >> 5)', i.e. to
32:#  that same port INCLUDING those two bits.  So there is no way to address ONE port through two
33:#  different lanes: the lane is a FUNCTION of the port.  The defect therefore partitions the whole
34:#  64 K ISA port space by `port & 3', and for a BYTE (len == 1) access it reads:
35:#
36:#      port & 3 == 0   ->  ofs 0.  data[0] = byte.                        CORRECT
37:#      port & 3 == 1   ->  ofs 1.  1 > 1 is FALSE, so ACCEPTED -- and the packing loop runs
38:#                          `for (i = 0; i < 1; i++) data[i] = (i == 1)? byte : 0', which is
39:#                          never true, so THE DEVICE BYTE IS DISCARDED AND THE GUEST IS HANDED
40:#                          ZERO with a success return.  A false success, not a decline.
41:#      port & 3 == 2   ->  ofs 2.  2 > 1  ->  fatal() + exit(1).          HOST DEATH
42:#      port & 3 == 3   ->  ofs 3.  3 > 1  ->  fatal() + exit(1).          HOST DEATH
43:#
44:#  For len == 2 the same arithmetic gives ofs 2 a zero answer and ofs 3 a death; for len 4 and 8
45:#  `ofs > len' is never true and the packing index is always in range, so those widths are clean.
46:#  The guard's `>' (rather than `>=') is what admits the zero-answering case: `ofs == len' passes
47:#  the guard and then indexes nothing.
48:#
49:#  WHAT THAT COSTS AT A REAL DEVICE, and it is why the ns16550 is the right subject.  The console
50:#  UART sits at ISA 0x3f8..0x3ff, so its eight registers fall into all four classes:
51:#
52:#      0x3f8 data     ofs 0   ok        0x3fc mcr       ofs 0   ok
53:#      0x3f9 ier      ofs 1   ZERO      0x3fd lsr       ofs 1   ZERO
54:#      0x3fa iir      ofs 2   DEATH     0x3fe msr       ofs 2   DEATH
55:#      0x3fb lctl     ofs 3   DEATH     0x3ff scratch   ofs 3   DEATH
56:#
57:#  A byte read of the LINE STATUS REGISTER -- the register a polling console driver reads before
58:#  every character -- returns zero, and a byte read of the MODEM STATUS or LINE CONTROL register
59:#  ends the emulator.  No unusual value, no driver setup, four guest instructions.
60:#
61:#  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
62:#  *** #530: IT IS NOW THE WITNESS AND THE DETECTOR.  Sessions 1-3 are the witness below, unchanged but
63:#  for the sentinel; the #530 sessions at the end are the detector for the fix. ***
64:#
65:#  THE FIX (disposition B, regress/artifacts/lcaisalane/FABLE_F2_RULING_20260914.md): the byte for port
66:#  P sits at buffer position (P & 3) % len on BOTH arms; `len == 0' is refused first; no latch, no
67:#  announce (there is no event -- member 4, ACCEPT).  Table 1 (37 rows): HEAD 19/37, fix 37/37
68:#  (regress/artifacts/lcaisalane/fix530_20260914/HEAD_det.out, FIX_det.out); after the pass-2 repair
69:#  (51 rows) see that dir's table 2; after closing pass 1's class closure (77 rows) its table 3; after
70:#  closing pass 2's tail cells and phantom-read rows (93 rows) its table 4; after closing pass 3's
71:#  fallthrough rows (111 rows) its table 5; after closing pass 4's forward-count CLASS CLOSURE (185 rows) its table 6.
72:#
73:#  THE CELL SPACE, rowed WHOLE since closing pass 2 (the direct and head cells since closing pass 1, the
74:#  tail cells since closing pass 2; pass 2 and closing pass 1 found the same class --
75:#  a (len, lane, direction) cell of the position rule with no row -- one cell over each time, so the
76:#  repair rows the cross rather than the next cell): direct widths len 1, 2, 4, 8 x lane 0-3 x R/W,
77:#  every cell rowed (the read side of len 4 at lanes 2/3 FULL-register, not only a single-lane mask);
78:#  split HEADS len 1-7 at lane 3 x R/W (a head ends at a port 0x1f mod 0x20; this probe's is 0x3ff);
79:#  split TAILS len 1-7 at lane 0 x R/W (a tail starts at the next port, 0 mod 0x20) -- tails of len 1,
80:#  2 and 4 are the direct lane-0 cells, and tails of len 3, 5, 6 and 7 are rowed at the 8042 DATA port
81:#  0x60 (sessions 4f `tailr' / `tailw', since closing pass 2).  *** THIS SAID "split TAILS start at port
82:#  0x400, where nothing is mapped, so a tail cell shows only as a whole-access failure ... not rowed per
83:#  length" UNTIL CLOSING PASS 2, AND IT WAS MEASURED FALSE: tails start at EVERY port 0 mod 0x20 (the
84:#  8259 at 0x20/0xa0, the 8253 at 0x40, the 8042 at 0x60), and the Opus seat's tail mis-placement
85:#  mutant scored 77/77 because the split rows' tails at the unmapped 0x400 can show a decline but never
86:#  a position. ***
87:#
88:#  CONTRACT (clause e) -- the detector is DESIGNED to catch, on EITHER arm, at every cell of that space:
89:#  a byte placed at any position other than (P & 3) % len (a single-cell mis-decode included -- the
90:#  Opus closing seat's c1_w2, c1_w1w, c1_r4 each scored 51/51 before this repair); and, by name: the
91:#  removed exit reinstated at any of the six cells that ended the host (reads AND
92:#  writes at (1,2) (1,3) (2,3)); a decline beyond the width or at-and-beyond it, or of any lane-0 wide
93:#  access (a store dropped, a load's register kept); a store arm narrowed to len <= 2 or its stores
94:#  dropped or forwarded to another port; one arm folding and the other not; the byte placed at position 0
95:#  instead of (P & 3) % len (the clamp, anchored on (2,1) == (2,3)); a lane decode that drops bit 1 or
96:#  the `& 3', on the read arm or the write arm; `& (len - 1)' for `% len' (the len-3/5 split heads); a
97:#  byte replicated into every position, at len 2, 4 or 8; the read arm's success return turned into a
98:#  failure; the write arm's `return' removed, so a store falls into the read arm and makes a phantom
99:#  read of the stored port (x_wfallthru), and the read arm's forward DUPLICATED (RD2, a second read) --
100:#  *** THIS BLOCK SAID THOSE TWO ARE `together THE FORWARD-COUNT CLASS, CLOSED BY ENUMERATION SINCE REPAIR 5 ... in
