`RET` checks out: the generated program returns to instruction 18 at `0xfffffc0001040048`. I also found a constraint for a future sweep: a write-arm variant that falls into the read arm overwrites the GETENV source string, which can shrink later requests. Each case needs fresh source state if its intended width is to remain reliable.

